[2026-09-20 10:42:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 022] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-20 10:42:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 022]   TEP / Planet-9 -- step 04: two real edges in the outer solar system
[2026-09-20 10:42:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 022]   Under TEP a field domain boundary is literally a wall in the clock
[2026-09-20 10:42:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 022]   structure: dynamics change character across it.  The solar system
[2026-09-20 10:42:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 022]   contains two sharp, unexplained radial edges that are candidate
[2026-09-20 10:42:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 022]   boundary signatures:
[2026-09-20 10:42:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 022]   E1  The Kuiper cliff.  The classical Kuiper belt's radial density
[2026-09-20 10:42:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 022]   ends abruptly near 47-50 AU (Trujillo & Brown 2001; Allen,
[2026-09-20 10:42:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 022]   Bernstein & Malhotra 2001; Petit+ 2011).  No accepted
[2026-09-20 10:42:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 022]   explanation: a smooth truncation event is too soft, a hidden
[2026-09-20 10:42:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 022]   planet is post-hoc.  Here the semimajor-axis distribution of
[2026-09-20 10:42:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 022]   cold classical objects (i < 5 deg) is extracted from the full
[2026-09-20 10:42:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 022]   SBDB catalog and the edge location and sharpness are measured
[2026-09-20 10:42:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 022]   with a logistic-edge fit, separately for cold and hot classicals.
[2026-09-20 10:42:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 022]   E2  The detachment boundary.  Objects with a > 150 AU separate into
[2026-09-20 10:42:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 022]   Neptune-coupled (q <~ 38 AU) and detached (q >~ 40 AU) sets; the
[2026-09-20 10:42:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 022]   intermediate perihelion range is anomalously empty -- the
[2026-09-20 10:42:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 022]   "perihelion gap" that marks where perturbative access ends.  A
[2026-09-20 10:42:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 022]   field boundary selects by crossing: the gap is the wall's
[2026-09-20 10:42:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 022]   inner-edge signature.  The q-distribution edge is measured the
[2026-09-20 10:42:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 022]   same way.
[2026-09-20 10:42:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 022]   Also computed: the aphelion-distance distribution of the detached
[2026-09-20 10:42:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 022]   population, locating the outer edge of the affected zone.
[2026-09-20 10:42:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 022]   Outputs: results/step_04_edges.json,
[2026-09-20 10:42:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 022]   figures/supplementary/step_04_edges.png
